# --- Python ---
*__pycache__/
*.venv/
*venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Secrets ---
*.env
!.env.example
*instructions.txt

# --- Data / corpora (never commit source documents) ---
# ANCHORED. `*documents/` matched at any depth and silently swallowed
# frontend/src/app/documents/ and frontend/src/components/documents/ — source
# files that were therefore never committed, so a clean clone could not build.
# Only the ingest scratch directory is data; the rest are code.
/backend/documents/
!backend/eval/corpus/
*minio_downloads/
*.ipynb

# --- Model weights & caches (fastembed / HuggingFace / ONNX) ---
# These are baked into the image at build time; they must never enter git.
# ANCHORED for the same reason: unanchored `models/` matched backend/models/,
# the Pydantic schema package and a documented architectural layer, which was
# therefore never committed. Weights on the host are covered by the extension
# patterns below; the image cache lives at /opt/models, not in the repo.
/models/
.cache/huggingface/
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.bin

# --- Node / Next.js ---
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
# TypeScript's incremental build cache ("incremental": true in tsconfig.json).
# It was committed once by accident. It is regenerated by every `tsc` run, so
# tracking it produces diff noise in unrelated commits -- and because
# frontend/Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, a tracked copy carries one developer's
# host-specific build state into the image build.
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# transient commit-message scratch
commit_msg.tmp
